"The file presents a sensitivity matrix covering two power levels (80% and 90%)","passed":true,"reasoning":"The Sample_Size sheet contains a sensitivity matrix titled \"Sensitivity matrix - total enrollment (with OBF GSD inflation and 15% dropout), empirical control rate 0.196, by power and absolute risk reduction\". The matrix lists rows for 80% and 90% power, satisfying the requirement for two power levels.","evidence":"Rows labeled 80% and 90% in the matrix"},{"index":1,"criterion":"The matrix covers two absolute risk reductions: 3% (p1=0.12) and 5% (p1=0.10)","passed":true,"reasoning":"The matrix includes columns for 3% and 5% absolute risk reductions (ARR), matching the specified effect sizes of 3% (p1=0.12) and 5% (p1=0.10).","evidence":"Columns labeled 3% and 5% in the matrix"},{"index":2,"criterion":"Both unadjusted and interim-analysis-adjusted calculations are included","passed":true,"reasoning":"The sheet provides both unadjusted per-group sample sizes (column \"N per group (unadjusted)\") and adjusted totals that include O'Brien-Fleming group sequential inflation and dropout inflation, demonstrating inclusion of interim-analysis-adjusted calculations.","evidence":"Columns \"N per group (unadjusted)\", \"Total (unadjusted)\", \"Total w/ OBF GSD inflation\", and \"Total to enroll (w/ 15% dropout)\""},{"index":3,"criterion":"There are exactly 8 distinct scenarios, each with computed per-group and total sample sizes","passed":false,"reasoning":"While the file lists 8 distinct scenarios (4 explicit scenarios plus 4 from the sensitivity matrix), the sensitivity matrix entries provide only total enrollment figures, not per-group sample sizes. The rubric requires each scenario to have both per-group and total sample sizes, which is not fully met.","evidence":"Sensitivity matrix rows show only total enrollment numbers (e.g., 6174, 3394, 2120, 1435) without per-group values"}],"overall_reasoning":"The rubric fails because criterion 3 is not satisfied: the sensitivity matrix does not provide per-group sample sizes for all 8 scenarios, only total enrollment figures."}},{"index":3,"rubric":"Does Baseline_Subgroup_Analysis.xlsx correctly stratify the eligible population by all four pre-specified subgroups (age groups, gender, baseline risk tertiles, smoking status)?","weight":10,"result":{"passed":false,"score":0,"criteria_count":5,"criteria_passed":4,"criteria_results":[{"index":0,"criterion":"The analysis stratifies the 1,108 operationally eligible subjects by age groups (reasonable categories such as 45-54, 55-64, 65-70 or similar)","passed":true,"reasoning":"The Subgroup_Baseline sheet lists age group strata 45-54, 55-64, 65-70 with corresponding N values.","evidence":"Age group,45-54,572; Age group,55-64,468; Age group,65-70,68"},{"index":1,"criterion":"The analysis stratifies by gender (male vs female using the 'male' variable)","passed":true,"reasoning":"Gender strata are present as Sex Female and Sex Male with N values.","evidence":"Sex,Female,645; Sex,Male,463"},{"index":2,"criterion":"The analysis stratifies by baseline Framingham Risk Score tertiles (calculated or approximated)","passed":false,"reasoning":"The sheet does not provide Framingham Risk Score tertiles; it only shows cholesterol tertiles as a proxy, which does not satisfy the requirement for baseline risk score stratification.","evidence":"Cholesterol tertile,Low chol tertile,368; Cholesterol tertile,Mid chol tertile,364; Cholesterol tertile,High chol tertile,366"},{"index":3,"criterion":"The analysis stratifies by smoking status (using currentSmoker variable)","passed":true,"reasoning":"Smoking status strata are present as Smoking Current smoker and Smoking Non-smoker with N values.","evidence":"Smoking,Current smoker,457; Smoking,Non-smoker,651"},{"index":4,"criterion":"Each stratum is clearly identified with its sample size","passed":true,"reasoning":"Each stratum row includes an explicit N column indicating sample size.","evidence":"All rows in Subgroup_Baseline contain an N value"}],"overall_reasoning":"All criteria except the baseline Framingham Risk Score tertile stratification are met; the absence of explicit risk score tertiles causes the rubric to fail."}},{"index":4,"rubric":"Does the analysis flag subgroups with fewer than 30 subjects as insufficient for meaningful subgroup analysis per FDA E9 guidance?","weight":10,"result":{"passed":false,"score":0,"criteria_count":3,"criteria_passed":0,"criteria_results":[{"index":0,"criterion":"The analysis identifies any subgroup strata with fewer than 30 subjects","passed":false,"reasoning":"The analysis does not identify any subgroup strata with fewer than 30 subjects; all reported N values are 68 or greater.","evidence":"Subgroup_Baseline sheet lists N values: 572, 468, 68, 645, 463, 457, 651, 490, 373, 245, 368, 364, 366 – none are <30."},{"index":1,"criterion":"Such strata are explicitly flagged as potentially underpowered for meaningful subgroup analysis","passed":false,"reasoning":"Because no strata <30 were identified, the analysis does not flag any such strata as underpowered; the only flagging refers to a stratum with N=68, which is not <30.","evidence":"Effect_Modification sheet contains an 'Insufficient strata' row stating the 65‑70 age stratum (N=68) is flagged INSUFFICIENT N, but no strata <30 are flagged."},{"index":2,"criterion":"The flagging references FDA E9 Section 5.7 principles that pre-specified subgroup analyses require adequate sample sizes to be interpretable","passed":false,"reasoning":"The flagging text does not reference FDA E9 Section 5.7; it cites other sections (5.3, 3.5, 4.3) but not 5.7.","evidence":"Flagging statements mention ICH E9 Section 5.3 (missing values), 3.5 (sample size), and 4.3 (interim analysis), but contain no reference to Section 5.7."}],"overall_reasoning":"All three criteria fail: no strata <30 were identified, no such strata were flagged, and the flagging does not cite FDA E9 Section 5.7."}},{"index":5,"rubric":"Does the analysis calculate mean and standard deviation of sysBP, totChol, and BMI for each subgroup stratum?","weight":6,"result":{"passed":false,"score":0,"criteria_count":3,"criteria_passed":0,"criteria_results":[{"index":0,"criterion":"For each subgroup stratum (age groups, gender, risk tertiles, smoking status), the analysis computes and reports mean and standard deviation of sysBP (systolic blood pressure)","passed":false,"reasoning":"The Subgroup_Baseline sheet lists a single sysBP value per stratum (e.g., 141 for age 45-54) but does not provide a standard deviation or any measure of variability. The rubric requires both mean and standard deviation for each subgroup stratum, which is not present.","evidence":"Subgroup_Baseline sheet: columns include sysBP (mmHg) but no SD column; only one numeric value per stratum."},{"index":1,"criterion":"For each subgroup stratum, the analysis computes and reports mean and standard deviation of totChol (total cholesterol)","passed":false,"reasoning":"Similarly, the sheet provides a single total cholesterol value per stratum (e.g., 246 for age 45-54) without a standard deviation. The rubric requires mean and SD for totChol, which is missing.","evidence":"Subgroup_Baseline sheet: column Total cholesterol (mg/dL) shows a single value per stratum; no SD column."},{"index":2,"criterion":"For each subgroup stratum, the analysis computes and reports mean and standard deviation of BMI","passed":false,"reasoning":"The BMI column also contains only a single mean value per stratum (e.g., 26.4 for age 45-54) and lacks a standard deviation. Thus the requirement for mean and SD of BMI is unmet.","evidence":"Subgroup_Baseline sheet: column BMI (kg/m2) shows a single value per stratum; no SD column."}],"overall_reasoning":"All three criteria require reporting both mean and standard deviation for sysBP, totChol, and BMI across each subgroup stratum. The provided Subgroup_Baseline sheet only supplies single mean values for each variable and contains no standard deviation columns. Consequently, none of the criteria are satisfied, and the rubric does not pass."}},{"index":6,"rubric":"Does the missing data assessment correctly identify glucose as having the highest missingness rate at approximately 9.3% (103/1108) in the operationally eligible population?","weight":10,"result":{"passed":false,"score":0,"criteria_count":3,"criteria_passed":0,"criteria_results":[{"index":0,"criterion":"The analysis reports the proportion of missing data for each variable in the eligible population","passed":false,"reasoning":"Failed to get judge response: Could not extract JSON from response: {\"criteria_results\":[{\"index\":0,\"passed\":true,\"reasoning\":\"The Missing_Data sheet lists each variable with its number of missing values and the corresponding percentage missing, covering all variables in the eligible population.\",\"evidence\":\"Variable,N missing,% missing\\nglucose,388,9.15\\neducation,105,2.48\\nBPMeds,53,1.25\\ntotChol,50,1.18\\ncigsPerDay,29,0.68\\nBMI,19,0.45\\nheartRate,1,0.02\"},\"{\"index\":1,\"passed\":false,\"reasoning\":\"The assessment reports glucose as the highest missingness variabl","evidence":""},{"index":1,"criterion":"The glucose variable is identified as having the highest missingness rate at approximately 9.3% (103 missing out of 1,108 operationally eligible subjects)","passed":false,"reasoning":"Failed to get judge response: Could not extract JSON from response: {\"criteria_results\":[{\"index\":0,\"passed\":true,\"reasoning\":\"The Missing_Data sheet lists each variable with its number of missing values and the corresponding percentage missing, covering all variables in the eligible population.\",\"evidence\":\"Variable,N missing,% missing\\nglucose,388,9.15\\neducation,105,2.48\\nBPMeds,53,1.25\\ntotChol,50,1.18\\ncigsPerDay,29,0.68\\nBMI,19,0.45\\nheartRate,1,0.02\"},\"{\"index\":1,\"passed\":false,\"reasoning\":\"The assessment reports glucose as the highest missingness variabl","evidence":""},{"index":2,"criterion":"Other variables with notable missingness (education, BPMeds, totChol, BMI) are also reported","passed":false,"reasoning":"Failed to get judge response: Could not extract JSON from response: {\"criteria_results\":[{\"index\":0,\"passed\":true,\"reasoning\":\"The Missing_Data sheet lists each variable with its number of missing values and the corresponding percentage missing, covering all variables in the eligible population.\",\"evidence\":\"Variable,N missing,% missing\\nglucose,388,9.15\\neducation,105,2.48\\nBPMeds,53,1.25\\ntotChol,50,1.18\\ncigsPerDay,29,0.68\\nBMI,19,0.45\\nheartRate,1,0.02\"},\"{\"index\":1,\"passed\":false,\"reasoning\":\"The assessment reports glucose as the highest missingness variabl","evidence":""}],"overall_reasoning":"Failed after 3 attempts: Could not extract JSON from response: {\"criteria_results\":[{\"index\":0,\"passed\":true,\"reasoning\":\"The Missing_Data sheet lists each variable with its number of missing values and the corresponding percentage missing, covering all variables in the eligible population.\",\"evidence\":\"Variable,N missing,% missing\\nglucose,388,9.15\\neducation,105,2.48\\nBPMeds,53,1.25\\ntotChol,50,1.18\\ncigsPerDay,29,0.68\\nBMI,19,0.45\\nheartRate,1,0.02\"},\"{\"index\":1,\"passed\":false,\"reasoning\":\"The assessment reports glucose as the highest missingness variabl"}},{"index":7,"rubric":"Does Eligibility_Analysis.xlsx document the number of subjects excluded by each criterion in a CONSORT-style population flow?","weight":8,"result":{"passed":true,"score":8,"criteria_count":5,"criteria_passed":5,"criteria_results":[{"index":0,"criterion":"The file includes a population flow showing the total Framingham dataset size (4,240 subjects)","passed":true,"reasoning":"The Population_Flow sheet lists the source cohort with 4,240 subjects.","evidence":"Source cohort (Framingham Heart Study),4240,0,4240"},{"index":1,"criterion":"The flow shows 2,813 subjects after the age criterion and 1,166 after the sysBP criterion","passed":true,"reasoning":"The flow shows 2,813 after age inclusion and 1,166 after systolic BP inclusion.","evidence":"Inclusion: age 45-70 years,4240,1427,2813; Inclusion: sysBP 130-159 mmHg,2813,1647,1166"},{"index":2,"criterion":"The flow then applies the observable proposal exclusions in a documented order: prevalentStroke=0 leaves 1,152 subjects and diabetes=0 leaves a final operationally eligible population of 1,108","passed":true,"reasoning":"The flow documents exclusions for prevalentStroke and diabetes in order, yielding 1,152 and 1,108 respectively.","evidence":"Exclusion: prevalentStroke = 1,1166,14,1152; Exclusion: diabetes = 1,1152,44,1108"},{"index":3,"criterion":"The flow explicitly notes that chronic kidney disease and broader prior-CVD history cannot be evaluated because the required fields are unavailable","passed":true,"reasoning":"The flow notes that CKD and broader prior-CVD cannot be evaluated due to missing fields.","evidence":"Notes: \"dataset has no broader prior-CVD indicator\"; Limitations sheet: CKD exclusion NOT OPERATIONALIZABLE"},{"index":4,"criterion":"The flow enables verification of the filtering process and assessment of generalizability","passed":true,"reasoning":"The flow provides step‑by‑step counts and notes, allowing verification and assessment of generalizability.","evidence":"Population_Flow sheet shows N before, excluded, remaining, and operationalization notes; Limitations sheet explains constraints"}],"overall_reasoning":"All five criteria are satisfied by the information in Eligibility_Analysis.xlsx, so the rubric passes."}}],"task_dir":"/Users/cmunley/Documents/Codex/2026-09-02/g/work/Gym/cache/huggingface/hub/datasets--JobBench--job-bench/snapshots/7ff2673ac78f42e492b204f5fffe0b8ccc11bf7d/dataset/biostatisticians/task1","rubrics_file":"/Users/cmunley/Documents/Codex/2026-09-02/g/work/Gym/cache/huggingface/hub/datasets--JobBench--job-bench/snapshots/7ff2673ac78f42e492b204f5fffe0b8cc