cting behaviour with the system package manager. It is recommended to use a virtual environment instead: https://pip.pypa.io/warnings/venv\n","type":"function_call_output","id":null,"status":null},{"id":"rs_72fc2a2a1d4a423cb581669f076de8a9","summary":[{"text":"Packages installed. Now I need the UCI Diabetes 130-US Hospitals dataset. The task says to obtain \"diabetic_data.csv\" from https://archive.ics.uci.edu/dataset/296. Also references \"sample_size_clinical_trials.pdf\" as external reference on sample size estimation — that file is not in /workspace/task, so I should search the web for it (instructions say \"If required information is absent, search the web\"). Actually, the sample size formula from Chow, Shao & Wang for two-sample parallel-group means is well known: n = (z_{α/2} + z_β)^2 * 2σ² / Δ² per group. I can apply that directly, and optionally try to fetch the PDF. Let me first try to download the UCI dataset.","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning","encrypted_content":null,"content":null},{"arguments":"{\"command\": \"cd /workspace/task && curl -sL -o diabetes130.zip \\\"https://archive.ics.uci.edu/static/public/296/diabetes+130+us+hospitals+for+years+1999+2008.zip\\\" && ls -la diabetes130.zip && unzip -o -q diabetes130.zip && ls -la\", \"description\": \"Download UCI Diabetes 130-US hospitals dataset\", \"timeout\": 120000}","call_id":"bash_0_76bd9dac","name":"bash","type":"function_call","id":null,"status":null,"namespace":null},{"call_id":"bash_0_76bd9dac","output":"-rw-r--r--. 1 root root 9 Sep  3 21:03 diabetes130.zip\n[diabetes130.zip]\n  End-of-central-directory signature not found.  Either this file is not\n  a zipfile, or it constitutes one disk of a multi-part archive.  In the\n  latter case the central directory and zipfile comment will be found on\n  the last disk(s) of this archive.\nunzip:  cannot find zipfile directory in one of diabetes130.zip or\n        diabetes130.zip.zip, and cannot find diabetes130.zip.ZIP, period.\n","type":"function_call_output","id":null,"status":null},{"arguments":"{\"command\": \"cd /workspace/task && rm diabetes130.zip && curl -sL -o diabetes130.zip \\\"https://archive.ics.uci.edu/static/public/296/diabetes+130-us+hospitals+for+years+1999-2008.zip\\\" && ls -la diabetes130.zip && file diabetes130.zip\", \"description\": \"Try alternate UCI download URL\", \"timeout\": 120000}","call_id":"bash_0_aa0a5279","name":"bash","type":"function_call","id":null,"status":null,"namespace":null},{"call_id":"bash_0_aa0a5279","output":"-rw-r--r--. 1 root root 3170254 Sep  3 21:03 diabetes130.zip\n/usr/bin/bash: line 1: file: command not found\n","type":"function_call_output","id":null,"status":null},{"arguments":"{\"command\": \"cd /workspace/task && unzip -o -q diabetes130.zip && ls -la\", \"description\": \"Unzip UCI diabetes dataset\"}","call_id":"bash_0_35345cbd","name":"bash","type":"function_call","id":null,"status":null,"namespace":null},{"call_id":"bash_0_35345cbd","output":"total 21904\ndrwxr-xr-x. 2  501 staff     4096 Sep  3 21:04 .\ndrwxr-xr-x. 1 root root        44 Sep  3 21:03 ..\n-rw-r--r--. 1  501 staff     2010 Sep  3 05:47 DX24_301_protocol_synopsis.csv\n-rw-r--r--. 1  501 staff    79529 Sep  3 05:47 DX24_phase3_trial_data.csv\n-rw-r--r--. 1 root root      2547 Jul 12  2023 IDS_mapping.csv\n-rw-r--r--. 1  501 staff     3201 Sep  3 05:47 TASK_INSTRUCTIONS.txt\n-rw-r--r--. 1 root root   3170254 Sep  3 21:03 diabetes130.zip\n-rw-r--r--. 1 root root  19159383 Jul 12  2023 diabetic_data.csv\n","type":"function_call_output","id":null,"status":null},{"id":"rs_fc0a7bd0761f4a29942dad456288b974","summary":[{"text":"The UCI dataset is downloaded. The local IDS_mapping.csv already existed in /workspace/task (matches the downloaded one apparently, since unzip overwrote it — same file). Note the IDS_mapping.csv in task was the reference file; the zip also contains IDS_mapping.csv. Fine.\n\nTask also references \"sample_size_clinical_trials.pdf\" as external reference — it's not