     -1.166667 -3.700000e-01 -0.796667\n118           -1.088889 -3.000000e-01 -0.788889\n109           -1.200000 -4.222222e-01 -0.777778\n102           -0.784615 -2.857143e-02 -0.756044\n121           -1.015385 -2.636364e-01 -0.751748\n111           -1.144444 -5.375000e-01 -0.606944\n122           -0.725000 -1.909091e-01 -0.534091\n","type":"function_call_output","id":null,"status":null},{"id":"rs_95c1d7e416394920a7f3d2eb88601c00","summary":[{"text":"Site 112 has the largest effect (-1.74), site 119 second (-1.69). Interesting. But wait — the concern is one site with an atypically large treatment effect. Site 112 = -1.74 is somewhat larger but not dramatically. Hmm, maybe per-subject ANCOVA per site would differ. Let me check per-site with adjusted analysis. Actually let me just check whether site 112 stands out more clearly with per-site means or maybe one site has a much bigger effect. Site 112 vs 119: -1.74 vs -1.69, close. Hmm.\n\nWait — maybe the outlier is more visible if looking at effect in another way. Let me look more carefully. Also possible that one site has a huge placebo response... Actually let me check per-site distributions more carefully — maybe there's something like one site with n=28 and effect much larger. Let's compute with proper CI per site. Let me just proceed with the analysis; the largest effect site is 112.\n\nHmm, but -1.74 vs -1.69 isn't \"atypical\". Let me check raw week 24 completer values without LOCF and also check whether the largest effect might be bigger with ANCOVA adjustment.","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning","encrypted_content":null,"content":null},{"arguments":"{\"command\": \"cd /workspace/task && python3 -c \\\"\\nimport pandas as pd, numpy as np\\ndf = pd.read_csv('DX24_phase3_trial_data.csv')\\n# completers only\\nc = df.dropna(subset=['hba1c_week24']).copy()\\nc['chg'] = c.hba1c_week24 - c.hba1c_baseline\\ng = c.groupby(['site_id','treatment_arm'])['chg'].agg(['mean','std','count']).reset_index()\\np = g.pivot(index='site_id', columns='treatment_arm', values='mean')\\np['eff'] = p['Drug_X'] - p['Placebo']\\nprint(p.sort_values('eff').head(5))\\nprint()\\n# per-subject check site 112\\ns = c[c.site_id==112]\\nprint(s.groupby('treatment_arm')['chg'].describe())\\n\\\"\\n\", \"description\": \"Check site effects with completers\"}","call_id":"bash_0_b236cd27","name":"bash","type":"function_call","id":null,"status":null,"namespace":null},{"call_id":"bash_0_b236cd27","output":"treatment_arm    Drug_X   Placebo       eff\nsite_id                                    \n124           -1.420000  0.480000 -1.900000\n112           -1.490000  0.250000 -1.740000\n119           -1.555556  0.133333 -1.688889\n107           -1.433333  0.070000 -1.503333\n106           -1.431250  0.057143 -1.488393\n\n               count  mean       std  min    25%   50%    75%  max\ntreatment_arm                                                     \nDrug_X          10.0 -1.49  0.597123 -2.3 -1.975 -1.55 -1.100 -0.5\nPlacebo          6.0  0.25  0.339116 -0.2  0.025  0.25  0.475  0.7\n","type":"function_call_output","id":null,"status":null},{"id":"rs_66e7e33a26a14c47aafafbf45bc3e35f","summary":[{"text":"Interesting - with completers only, site 124 is the largest (-1.90). With LOCF, site 112 is largest (-1.74). I should use ANCOVA-based per-site effects per protocol spec. Let me use the LOCF ITT dataset per protocol (\"ITT population with LOCF\") and ANCOVA within each site. Site 112 vs 124 — which is the outlier? With ANCOVA adjustment per site the answer may change. Let me run ANCOVA per site.","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning","encrypted_content":null,"content":null},{"arguments":"{\"command\": \"cd /workspace/task && python3 -c \\\"\\nimport pandas as pd, numpy as np\\nimport statsmodels.formula.api as smf\\ndf = pd.read_csv('DX24_phase3_trial_data.csv')\\ndf['hba1c_w24'] = df.hba1c_week24.fillna(df.hba1c_week12)\\ndf['chg'] = df.hba1c_w24 - df.hba1c_baseline\\nres=[]\\nfor s,g in df.groupby('site_id'):\\n    m = smf.ols('chg ~ treatment_arm + hba1c_baseline', data=g).fit()\\n    res.append((s, m.params['treatment_arm[T.Placebo]']*-1, m.bse['treatment_arm[T.Placebo]'], len(g)))\\nr = pd.DataFrame(res, columns=['site','effect','se','n']).sort_values('effect')\\nprint(r.to_string())\\n\\\"\\n\", \"description\": \"ANCOVA per-site treatment effects with LOCF\"}","call_id":"bash_0_ec952e75","name":"bash","type":"function_call","id":null,"status":null,"namespace":null},{"call_id":"bash_0_ec952e75","output":"    site    effect        se   n\n18   119 -1.835467  0.261603  15\n23   124 -1.627451  0.458883  12\n11   112 -1.596620  0.252629  16\n3    104 -1.476459  0.293927  28\n5    106 -1.454021  0.350288  26\n6    107 -1.450353  0.290296  16\n12   113 -1.431704  0.268138  12\n0    101 -1.383860  0.286506  16\n7    108 -1.262766  0.311534  16\n19   120 -1.230401  0.315351  25\n16   117 -1.212754  0.280383  25\n2    103 -1.192126  0.362959  19\n14   115 -1.190245  0.320580  20\n15   116 -1.180791  0.292742  23\n22   123 -1.142619  0.211218  21\n24   125 -1.040741  0.408507  20\n9    110 -0.880872  0.389301  17\n13   114 -0.871486  0.280838  21\n21   122 -0.807287  0.338191  15\n4    105 -0.786677  0.306365  21\n8    109 -0.763926  0.380123  16\n1    102 -0.762437  0.325615  20\n17   118 -0.729531  0.242427  17\n20   121 -0.719073  0.328718  26\n10   111 -0.689559  0.267117  17\n","type":"function_call_output","id":null,"status":null},{"id":"rs_a14593dd21fd4897aedc68f41d483574","summary":[{"text":"Site 119 is the outlier with the largest effect (-1.835, ANCOVA-adjusted, LOCF). Also raw completers showed site 124 with -1.9 but small n. The task says \"largest treatment effect on HbA1c change from baseline to Week 24\". Using the protocol's ANCOVA specification with LOCF, site 119 is the outlier. I'll go with site 119.\n\nNow build the full analysis script. Components:\n\n1. **Audit sheet**: protocol vs observed discrepancies:\n   - Planned Enrollment: 480 (240/arm) vs observed 480 (240/arm) — match\n   - Number of Sites: 25 vs 25 — match\n   - Age range 18-75 vs observed 30-75 — within range (no violations). Check for actual violations: age min 30, max 75 — OK.\n   - HbA1c baseline 7.0-10.5 vs observed 7.0-10.6 — one subject at 10.6 exceeds 10.5? Check how many >10.5.\n   - Assumed treatment difference -1.0% vs observed\n   - Assumed SD 1.2% vs observed pooled SD\n   - Dropout assumed 10% vs observed 42/480 = 8.75%... but check: 42 discontinued = 8.75%. Also ITT missing week24 = 42.\n   - Randomization 1:1 vs 240:240 — match\n   - Treatment duration 24 weeks\n   - Target population on stable metformin: prior_metformin 83.75% — 16.25% not on metformin = discrepancy (protocol says all on metformin)\n   - Primary analysis: ANCOVA, ITT with LOCF\n\n2. **Site Effects sheet**: per-site ANCOVA effects w/ 95% CI + LOSO results (overall ANCOVA excluding each site, effect + p-value).\n\n3. **Subgroup Forest**: mixed-effects model with site random effect, treatment × age group (<65/≥65), treatment × sex, baseline HbA1c. Report interaction p-values. Forest plot of subgroup treatment effects (age groups, sexes, overall). Save PNG, embed in sheet.\n\n4. **Sample Size**: two scenarios (full dataset effect, effect excl. site 119). Formula from Chow: n per arm = 2σ²(z_{α/2}+z_β)²/δ², target δ = 0.8×observed effect, 90% power, α=0.05 two-sided, observed pooled SD, 15% dropout inflation. Conditional power at week 24 given interim observed data.\n\nConditional power: treat current observed effect as interim. CP = P(reject H0 at end | observed trend). For a completed study... Simplest standard approach: conditional power = Φ((z_observed - z_{α/2}·something)...). Actually common definition: CP = Φ( (θ̂/θ_assumed... ) ). A standard formula: CP(c) = 1 - Φ( (z_{1-α/2} - z(t)·√c) / √(1-c) ) where z(t) is observed z at interim and c is the fraction of information remaining. Hmm.\n\nGiven the task: \"compute the conditional power of the current study at Week 24 given observed interim data\". A pragmatic approach: conditional power given observed effect = P(reject H0 | true effect = observed effect) using planned n and observed SD. That's essentially post-hoc power. Formula: CP = Φ( |δ_obs|√(n_per_arm/2)/σ - z_{1-α/2} ). That's a defensible \"conditional power at Week 24 given the observed data\". I'll document the formula.\n\nAlternatively conditional power under Chow's framework for two-sample means at final analysis assuming current trend continues: CP = Φ( -z_{α/2} + δ√n/(√2 σ) ) using observed δ. I'll use that with n = planned per-arm (240) and also maybe with observed completers. I'll compute with observed ITT n per arm and observed SD and effect — document it.\n\n5. **RWE Comparison**: diabetic_data.csv:\n   - A1C test proportions (A1Cresult column: values \"Norm\", \">7\", \">8\", \"None\") across admission types (decoded via IDS_mapping admission_type_id). Proportion tested = A1Cresult != \"None\".\n   - Medication utilization: metformin, insulin, GLP-1 agents. In diabetic_data there's no GLP-1 column... columns include metformin, insulin, and various others (glipizide, etc.). GLP-1 agents: the dataset has no GLP-1 RA column. Check columns. Actually there might be no exenatide/liraglutide. I'll check. If absent, note 0%/not captured (dataset predates widespread GLP-1 use). Trial baseline: prior_metformin 83.75%, prior_insulin 13.33%, prior GLP-1 = 0% (Drug X is investigational, patients GLP-1-naive).\n   \n   Compare: trial prior_metformin 83.8% vs RWE metformin utilization (any of Up/Down/Steady). Insulin: 13.3% vs RWE insulin utilization. GLP-1: 0% in trial (exclusion — investigational class) vs ~0% in RWE (not captured in dataset).\n\nDeliverables: only the Excel workbook in /workspace/output. \"save only final deliverables\" — so the xlsx (with embedded forest plot PNG). I'll create forest plot PNG in output? \"save only final deliverables in /workspace/output\" — the workbook is the deliverable; embed the PNG into the sheet and don't leave stray files (or keep PNG? Safer to embed and remove the PNG, or keep PNG in a temp dir). I'll write PNG to /tmp and embed.\n\nLet me now check trial data details for audit: baseline HbA1c >10.5 count, missing week24, race distribution, countries unknown. Let me write the full script.","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning","encrypted_content":null,"content":null},{"id":"msg_125c8b6a8d694da0a60ddd9bc92acfc2","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"Site 119 is the outlier (largest ANCOVA-adjusted effect, -1.84%). Now I'll write the full analysis script.","type":"output_text","logprobs":null}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":null},{"arguments":"{\"command\": \"cd /workspace/task && python3 -c \\\"\\nimport pandas as pd\\nd = pd.read_csv('diabetic_data.csv')\\nprint(d.shape)\\nprint([c for c in d.columns])\\nprint(d.A1Cresult.value_counts(dropna=False).to_dict())\\nprint(d.admission_type_id.value_counts(dropna=False).to_dict())\\n\\\"\\n\", \"description\": \"Explore RWE dataset columns\"}","call_id":"bash_0_8b66e971","name":"bash","type":"function_call","id":null,"status":null,"namespace":null},{"call_id":"bash_0_8b66e971","output":"(101766, 50)\n['encounter_id', 'patient_nbr', 'race', 'gender', 'age', 'weight', 'admission_type_id', 'discharge_disposition_id', 'admission_source_id', 'time_in_hospital', 'payer_code', 'medical_specialty', 'num_lab_procedures', 'num_procedures', 'num_medications', 'number_outpatient', 'number_emergency', 'number_inpatient', 'diag_1', 'diag_2', 'diag_3', 'number_diagnoses', 'max_glu_serum', 'A1Cresult', 'metformin', 'repaglinide', 'nateglinide', 'chlorpropamide', 'glimepiride', 'acetohexamide', 'glipizide', 'glyburide', 'tolbutamide', 'pioglitazone', 'rosiglitazone', 'acarbose', 'miglitol', 'troglitazone', 'tolazamide', 'examide', 'citoglipton', 'insulin', 'glyburide-metformin', 'glipizide-metformin', 'glimepiride-pioglitazone', 'metformin-rosiglitazone', 'metformin-pioglitazone', 'change', 'diabetesMed', 'readmitted']\n{nan: 84748, '>8': 8216, 'Norm': 4990, '>7': 3812}\n{1: 53990, 3: 18869, 2: 18480, 6: 5291, 5: 4785, 8: 320, 7: 21, 4: 10}\n","type":"function_call_output","id":null,"status":null},{"id":"msg_bc34252b1da5457ab27c5ff31e9e0c9f","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"All data confirmed. Now writing the full analysis script.","type":"output_text","logprobs":null}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":null},{"arguments":"{\"content\": \"import pandas as pd\\nimport numpy as np\\nimport statsmodels.formula.api as smf\\nfrom scipy import stats\\nimport matplotlib\\nmatplotlib.use(\\\"Agg\\\")\\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\\nfrom openpyxl import Workbook\\nfrom openpyxl.drawing.image import Image as XLImage\\nfrom openpyxl.styles import Font, Alignment, PatternFill\\nfrom openpyxl.utils import get_column_letter\\n\\nTASK = \\\"/workspace/task\\\"\\nOUT = \\\"/workspace/output/DX24_301_Integrity_Analysis.xlsx\\\"\\n\\n# ---------------- Load data ----------------\\ntrial = pd.read_csv(f\\\"{TASK}/DX24_phase3_trial_data.csv\\\")\\nprot = pd.read_csv(f\\\"{TASK}/DX24_301_protocol_synopsis.csv\\\")\\nrwe = pd.read_csv(f\\\"{TASK}/diabetic_data.csv\\\")\\nids = pd.read_csv(f\\\"{TASK}/IDS_mapping.csv\\\")\\n\\ntrial[\\\"hba1c_w24_locf\\\"] = trial.hba1c_week24.fillna(trial.hba1c_week12)\\ntrial[\\\"chg\\\"] = trial.hba1c_w24_locf - trial.hba1c_baseline\\n\\n# ---------------- 1. Audit: protocol vs data ----------------\\naudit_rows = []\\ndef audit(param, protocol, observed, flag):\\n    audit_rows.append({\\\"Parameter\\\": param, \\\"Protocol Value\\\": protocol,\\n                       \\\"Observed Value\\\": observed, \\\"Discrepancy Flag\\\": flag})\\n\\naudit(\\\"Planned Enrollment\\\", \\\"480 (240 per arm)\\\",\\n      f\\\"{len(trial)} ({(trial.treatment_arm=='Drug_X').sum()} Drug X / {(trial.treatment_arm=='Placebo').sum()} Placebo)\\\",\\n      \\\"None\\\" if len(trial)==480 else \\\"DISCREPANCY\\\")\\naudit(\\\"Number of Sites\\\", \\\"25 sites across 5 countries\\\",\\n      f\\\"{trial.site_id.nunique()} sites (single country implied by site numbering)\\\",\\n      \\\"None\\\" if trial.site_id.nunique()==25 else \\\"DISCREPANCY\\\")\\naudit(\\\"Randomization Ratio\\\", \\\"1:1 (Drug X : Placebo)\\\",\\n      f\\\"{(trial.treatment_arm=='Drug_X').sum()}:{(trial.treatment_arm=='Placebo').sum()}\\\",\\n      \\\"None\\\")\\naudit(\\\"Age Range (18-75)\\\", \\\"18-75 years\\\",\\n      f\\\"{trial.age.min()}-{trial.age.max()} years (no subjects <18)\\\",\\n      \\\"Minor - lower bound underrepresented\\\" if trial.age.min()>18 else \\\"None\\\")\\naudit(\\\"HbA1c Inclusion (7.0-10.5%)\\\", \\\"7.0-10.5%\\\",\\n      f\\\"{trial.hba1c_baseline.min():.1f}-{trial.hba1c_baseline.max():.1f}%\\\",\\n      \\\"DISCREPANCY - subject(s) above 10.5%\\\" if trial.hba1c_baseline.max()>10.5 else \\\"None\\\")\\naudit(\\\"Target Population: on stable metformin\\\", \\\"100% on stable metformin\\\",\\n      f\\\"{(trial.prior_metformin=='Yes').mean()*100:.1f}% with prior metformin\\\",\\n      \\\"DISCREPANCY - not all subjects on metformin\\\" if (trial.prior_metformin=='Yes').mean()<1 else \\\"None\\\")\\ndisc_rate = (trial.discontinued=='Yes').mean()\\naudit(\\\"Dropout Rate Assumed\\\", \\\"10%\\\",\\n      f\\\"{disc_rate*100:.1f}% ({(trial.discontinued=='Yes').sum()} discontinued)\\\",\\n      \\\"None\\\" if disc_rate<=0.12 else \\\"DISCREPANCY - higher than assumed\\\")\\nmiss24 = trial.hba1c_week24.isna().sum()\\naudit(\\\"Missing Week 24 HbA1c (LOCF applied)\\\", \\\"n/a (LOCF prespecified)\\\",\\n      f\\\"{miss24} subjects ({miss24/len(trial)*100:.1f}%) missing Week 24; LOCF imputed\\\",\\n      \\\"Note\\\" if miss24>0 else \\\"None\\\")\\nw24_by_arm = trial[trial.hba1c_week24.isna()].treatment_arm.value_counts()\\naudit(\\\"Missingness by Arm (differential dropout)\\\",\\n      \\\"Balanced assumed\\\",\\n      f\\\"Drug X: {w24_by_arm.get('Drug_X',0)}, Placebo: {w24_by_arm.get('Placebo',0)}\\\",\\n      \\\"Note - higher dropout on Drug X\\\" if w24_by_arm.get('Drug_X',0) > w24_by_arm.get('Placebo',0)*1.25 else \\\"None\\\")\\n\\n# observed SD and effect for variability audit\\nsd_pool_obs = trial.groupby(\\\"treatment_arm\\\")[\\\"chg\\\"].std()\\npooled_sd = np.sqrt((((trial.treatment_arm=='Drug_X').sum()-1)*sd_pool_obs['Drug_X']**2 +\\n                     ((trial.treatment_arm=='Placebo').sum()-1)*sd_pool_obs['Placebo']**2) /\\n                    (len(trial)-2))\\naudit(\\\"Assumed Common SD (HbA1c change)\\\", \\\"1.2%\\\",\\n      f\\\"Observed pooled SD = {pooled_sd:.2f}%\\\",\\n      \\\"None\\\" if abs(pooled_sd-1.2)<=0.15 else \\\"Note - differs from assumption\\\")\\naudit(\\\"Assumed Treatment Difference\\\", \\\"-1.0%\\\",\\n      \\\"See Site Effects sheet\\\",\\n      \\\"None\\\")\\n\\n# ---------------- 2. Site effects (ANCOVA per site, ITT/LOCF) ----------------\\nsite_rows = []\\nfor s, g in trial.groupby(\\\"site_id\\\"):\\n    m = smf.ols(\\\"chg ~ treatment_arm + hba1c_baseline\\\", data=g).fit()\\n    est = m.params[\\\"treatment_arm[T.Placebo]\\\"]  # placebo - drugx; flip sign\\n    eff = -est\\n    se = m.bse[\\\"treatment_arm[T.Placebo]\\\"]\\n    ci = m.conf_int().loc[\\\"treatment_arm[T.Placebo]\\\"]\\n    site_rows.append({\\\"Site ID\\\": s, \\\"N\\\": len(g),\\n                      \\\"Treatment Effect (Drug X - Placebo)\\\": eff,\\n                      \\\"SE\\\": se,\\n                      \\\"95% CI Lower\\\": -ci[1], \\\"95% CI Upper\\\": -ci[0],\\n                      \\\"P-value\\\": m.pvalues[\\\"treatment_arm[T.Placebo]\\\"]})\\nsite_df = pd.DataFrame(site_rows).sort_values(\\\"Treatment Effect (Drug X - Placebo)\\\").reset_index(drop=True)\\noutlier_site = int(site_df.iloc[0][\\\"Site ID\\\"])\\n\\n# Overall ANCOVA\\nm_all = smf.ols(\\\"chg ~ treatment_arm + hba1c_baseline\\\", data=trial).fit()\\noverall_eff = -m_all.params[\\\"treatment_arm[T.Placebo]\\\"]\\noverall_p = m_all.pvalues[\\\"treatment_arm[T.Placebo]\\\"]\\noverall_ci = m_all.conf_int().loc[\\\"treatment_arm[T.Placebo]\\\"]\\noverall_ci = (-overall_ci[1], -overall_ci[0])\\n\\n# ---------------- 3. Leave-one-site-out ----------------\\nloso_rows = [{\\\"Excluded Site\\\": \\\"None (Full Data)\\\", \\\"N\\\": len(trial),\\n              \\\"Treatment Difference\\\": overall_eff, \\\"95% CI Lower\\\": overall_ci[0],\\n              \\\"95% CI Upper\\\": overall_ci[1], \\\"P-value\\\": overall_p}]\\nfor s in sorted(trial.site_id.unique()):\\n    d = trial[trial.site_id != s]\\n    m = smf.ols(\\\"chg ~ treatment_arm + hba1c_baseline\\\", data=d).fit()\\n    eff = -m.params[\\\"treatment_arm[T.Placebo]\\\"]\\n    p = m.pvalues[\\\"treatment_arm[T.Placebo]\\\"]\\n    ci = m.conf_int().loc[\\\"treatment_arm[T.Placebo]\\\"]\\n    loso_rows.append({\\\"Excluded Site\\\": f\\\"Site {s}\\\" + (\\\" (OUTLIER)\\\" if s==outlier_site else \\\"\\\"),\\n                      \\\"N\\\": len(d), \\\"Treatment Difference\\\": eff,\\n                      \\\"95% CI Lower\\\": -ci[1], \\\"95% CI Upper\\\": -ci[0], \\\"P-value\\\": p})\\nloso_df = pd.DataFrame(loso_rows)\\n\\n# ---------------- 4. Mixed-effects model with random site + interactions ----------------\\ntrial[\\\"age_group\\\"] = np.where(trial.age >= 65, \\\">=65\\\", \\\"<65\\\")\\nmm = smf.mixedlm(\\n    \\\"chg ~ treatment_arm*age_group + treatment_arm*sex + hba1c_baseline\\\",\\n    data=trial, groups=trial[\\\"site_id\\\"]).fit(reml=True)\\nint_age_p = mm.pvalues.get(\\\"treatment_arm[T.Placebo]:age_group[<65]\\\", np.nan)\\nint_sex_p = mm.pvalues.get(\\\"treatment_arm[T.Placebo]:sex[T.Male]\\\", np.nan)\\nfixed = mm.params\\n\\n# Subgroup treatment effects for forest plot (ANCOVA within subgroup)\\ndef subgroup_effect(d, label, category):\\n    m = smf.ols(\\\"chg ~ treatment_arm + hba1c_baseline\\\", data=d).fit()\\n    eff = -m.params[\\\"treatment_arm[T.Placebo]\\\"]\\n    ci = m.conf_int().loc[\\\"treatment_arm[T.Placebo]\\\"]\\n    return {\\\"Subgroup\\\": category, \\\"Level\\\": label, \\\"N\\\": len(d),\\n            \\\"Treatment Effect\\\": eff, \\\"CI Lower\\\": -ci[1], \\\"CI Upper\\\": -ci[0],\\n            \\\"P-value\\\": m.pvalues[\\\"treatment_arm[T.Placebo]\\\"]}\\n\\nsg_rows = [\\n    subgroup_effect(trial[trial.age_group==\\\"<65\\\"], \\\"<65\\\", \\\"Age Group\\\"),\\n    subgroup_effect(trial[trial.age_group==\\\">=65\\\"], \\\">=65\\\", \\\"Age Group\\\"),\\n    subgroup_effect(trial[trial.sex==\\\"Female\\\"], \\\"Female\\\", \\\"Sex\\\"),\\n    subgroup_effect(trial[trial.sex==\\\"Male\\\"], \\\"Male\\\", \\\"Sex\\\"),\\n]\\nsg_df = pd.DataFrame(sg_rows)\\n\\n# ---------------- 5. Sample size & conditional power ----------------\\n# Reference: Chow, Shao & Wang - two-sample parallel means:\\n# n per group = 2 * sigma^2 * (z_{1-alpha/2} + z_{1-beta})^2 / delta^2\\nza = stats.norm.ppf(1 - 0.05/2)\\nzb = stats.norm.ppf(0.90)\\nsd = pooled_sd\\n\\ndef n_per_group(delta, sigma):\\n    return 2 * sigma**2 * (za + zb)**2 / delta**2\\n\\neff_full = abs(overall_eff)\\nexcl = trial[trial.site_id != outlier_site]\\nm_ex = smf.ols(\\\"chg ~ treatment_arm + hba1c_baseline\\\", data=excl).fit()\\neff_excl = abs(-m_ex.params[\\\"treatment_arm[T.Placebo]\\\"])\\np_excl = m_ex.pvalues[\\\"treatment_arm[T.Placebo]\\\"]\\n\\ndef scenario(effect_obs):\\n    target = 0.8 * effect_obs          # 80% of observed effect as target difference\\n    n_raw = n_per_group(target, sd)    # per group\\n    n_adj = np.ceil(n_raw / (1 - 0.15))  # 15% dropout adjustment\\n    return target, np.ceil(n_raw), int(n_adj), int(2*n_adj)\\n\\ntgt_full, n_full_raw, n_full, tot_full = scenario(eff_full)\\ntgt_excl, n_excl_raw, n_excl, tot_excl = scenario(eff_excl)\\n\\nss_rows = pd.DataFrame([\\n    {\\\"Parameter\\\": \\\"Target difference (80% of observed effect, %)\\\", \\\"Scenario A: Full Dataset\\\": round(tgt_full,3), \\\"Scenario B: Excluding Outlier Site\\\": round(tgt_excl,3)},\\n    {\\\"Parameter\\\": \\\"Observed treatment effect (%)\\\", \\\"Scenario A: Full Dataset\\\": round(eff_full,3), \\\"Scenario B: Excluding Outlier Site\\\": round(eff_excl,3)},\\n    {\\\"Parameter\\\": \\\"Pooled SD used (%)\\\", \\\"Scenario A: Full Dataset\\\": round(sd,3), \\\"Scenario B: Excluding Outlier Site\\\": round(sd,3)},\\n    {\\\"Parameter\\\": \\\"Power\\\", \\\"Scenario A: Full Dataset\\\": \\\"90%\\\", \\\"Scenario B: Excluding Outlier Site\\\": \\\"90%\\\"},\\n    {\\\"Parameter\\\": \\\"Two-sided alpha\\\", \\\"Scenario A: Full Dataset\\\": 0.05, \\\"Scenario B: Excluding Outlier Site\\\": 0.05},\\n    {\\\"Parameter\\\": \\\"N per group (before dropout)\\\", \\\"Scenario A: Full Dataset\\\": int(n_full_raw), \\\"Scenario B: Excluding Outlier Site\\\": int(n_excl_raw)},\\n    {\\\"Parameter\\\": \\\"N per group (15% dropout adj.)\\\", \\\"Scenario A: Full Dataset\\\": n_full, \\\"Scenario B: Excluding Outlier Site\\\": n_excl},\\n    {\\\"Parameter\\\": \\\"Total N (both arms)\\\", \\\"Scenario A: Full Dataset\\\": tot_full, \\\"Scenario B: Excluding Outlier Site\\\": tot_excl},\\n])\\n\\n# Conditional power at Week 24 given observed interim data.\\n# Observed effect so far: overall_eff (LOCF ANCOVA). Planned total N = 480 (reached).\\n# Conditional power = probability of rejecting H0 at final given current trend.\\n# Under a normal approximation with observed effect d and SE at final analysis:\\nse_final = sd * np.sqrt(2/(len(trial)/2))  # planned full sample\\nzcrit = za\\nobs_z = eff_full / (sd*np.sqrt(2/ (len(trial)/2)))  # observed z at current (full) N\\n# Since Week 24 data are already complete for ITT/LOCF, conditional power given\\n# observed data equals the power of the test at the observed effect size:\\ncond_power = stats.norm.cdf(obs_z - zcrit) + stats.norm.cdf(-obs_z - zcrit)\\n# More standard formulation (conditional on interim, projecting to final):\\n# CP = Phi( (d_obs * sqrt(n_final) / (sigma*sqrt(2)) - z_{1-a/2}) )\\ncp = stats.norm.cdf(eff_full*np.sqrt(len(trial)/2)/(sd*np.sqrt(2)) - zcrit)\\ncp += stats.norm.cdf(-eff_full*np.sqrt(len(trial)/2)/(sd*np.sqrt(2)) - zcrit)\\n\\n# ---------------- 6. RWE comparison ----------------\\nids_adm = ids.dropna(subset=[\\\"admission_type_id\\\"]).dropna(subset=[\\\"description\\\"])\\nids_adm = ids_adm[ids_adm[\\\"admission_type_id\\\"].astype(str).str.strip()!=\\\"\\\"]\\nadm_map = dict(zip(ids_adm[\\\"admission_type_id\\\"].astype(int), ids_adm[\\\"description\\\"]))\\nrwe[\\\"adm_label\\\"] = rwe.admission_type_id.map(adm_map).fillna(\\\"Other\\\")\\nrwe[\\\"a1c_tested\\\"] = rwe.A1Cresult.notna()\\n\\na1c_by_adm = rwe.groupby(\\\"adm_label\\\")[\\\"a1c_tested\\\"].agg([\\\"sum\\\",\\\"count\\\"])\\na1c_by_adm[\\\"pct_tested\\\"] = a1c_by_adm[\\\"sum\\\"]/a1c_by_adm[\\\"count\\\"]*100\\na1c_by_adm = a1c_by_adm.sort_values(\\\"count\\\", ascending=False)\\n\\nrwe_met = (rwe[\\\"metformin\\\"].isin([\\\"Up\\\",\\\"Down\\\",\\\"Steady\\\"])).mean()*100\\nrwe_ins = (rwe[\\\"insulin\\\"].isin([\\\"Up\\\",\\\"Down\\\",\\\"Steady\\\"])).mean()*100\\n# GLP-1 agents did not exist as a class in this dataset (era 1999-2008);\\n# exenatide (examide) column present but essentially unused.\\nrwe_glp1 = (rwe[\\\"examide\\\"].isin([\\\"Up\\\",\\\"Down\\\",\\\"Steady\\\"])).mean()*100\\n\\ntrial_met = (trial.prior_metformin==\\\"Yes\\\").mean()*100\\ntrial_ins = (trial.prior_insulin==\\\"Yes\\\").mean()*100\\n\\nrwe_med_rows = pd.DataFrame([\\n    {\\\"Medication\\\": \\\"Metformin\\\", \\\"RWE Cohort (% encounters on drug)\\\": round(rwe_met,2),\\n     \\\"DX24-301 Baseline History (%)\\\": round(trial_met,2)},\\n    {\\\"Medication\\\": \\\"Insulin\\\", \\\"RWE Cohort (% encounters on drug)\\\": round(rwe_ins,2),\\n     \\\"DX24-301 Baseline History (%)\\\": round(trial_ins,2)},\\n    {\\\"Medication\\\": \\\"GLP-1 agonists (exenatide in RWE)\\\", \\\"RWE Cohort (% encounters on drug)\\\": round(rwe_glp1,2),\\n     \\\"DX24-301 Baseline History (%)\\\": \\\"0 (excluded by design - study drug class)\\\"},\\n])\\n\\n# ---------------- Forest plot ----------------\\nfig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(8, 4.5))\\nylabels = []\\nfor i, r in sg_df.iterrows():\\n    ax.errorbar(r[\\\"Treatment Effect\\\"], i,\\n                xerr=[[r[\\\"Treatment Effect\\\"]-r[\\\"CI Lower\\\"]],[r[\\\"CI Upper\\\"]-r[\\\"Treatment Effect\\\"]]],\\n                fmt=\\\"o\\\", capsize=4, color=\\\"navy\\\")\\n    ylabels.append(f'{r[\\\"Subgroup\\\"]}: {r[\\\"Level\\\"]} (N={r[\\\"N\\\"]})')\\nax.axvline(overall_eff, color=\\\"red\\\", ls=\\\"--\\\", label=f\\\"Overall effect = {overall_eff:.2f}\\\")\\nax.axvline(0, color=\\\"gray\\\", ls=\\\"-\\\", lw=0.5)\\nax.set_yticks(range(len(sg_df)), ylabels)\\nax.invert_yaxis()\\nax.set_xlabel(\\\"HbA1c Change from Baseline, Drug X - Placebo (%)\\\")\\nax.set_title(\\\"Subgroup Treatment Effects (95% CI) - DX24-301\\\")\\nax.legend(loc=\\\"lower right\\\")\\nplt.tight_layout()\\nforest_png = \\\"/workspace/output/_forest_tmp.png\\\"\\nplt.savefig(forest_png, dpi=150)\\nplt.close()\\n\\n# ---------------- Write Excel ----------------\\nwb = Workbook()\\nhdr_fill = PatternFill(\\\"solid\\\", fgColor=\\\"D9E1F2\\\")\\nbold = Font(bold=True)\\n\\ndef write_df(ws, df, start_row=1, title=None):\\n    r = start_row\\n    if title:\\n        ws.cell(r, 1, title).font = Font(bold=True, size=12)\\n        r += 1\\n    for j, col in enumerate(df.columns, 1):\\n        c = ws.cell(r, j, col)\\n        c.font = bold\\n        c.fill = hdr_fill\\n        c.alignment = Alignment(wrap_text=True, vertical=\\\"top\\\")\\n    r += 1\\n    for _, row in df.iterrows():\\n        for j, col in enumerate(df.columns, 1):\\n            v = row[col]\\n            if isinstance(v, (np.integer,)): v = int(v)\\n            if isinstance(v, (np.floating,)): v = float(v)\\n            c = ws.cell(r, j, v)\\n            c.alignment = Alignment(wrap_text=True, vertical=\\\"top\\\")\\n        r += 1\\n    return r + 1\\n\\n# Sheet 1: Audit\\nws = wb.active\\nws.title = \\\"Audit\\\"\\naudit_df = pd.DataFrame(audit_rows)\\nwrite_df(ws, audit_df, title=\\\"Protocol-vs-Data Discrepancy Table - DX24-301\\\")\\n\\n# Sheet 2: Site Effects\\nws = wb.create_sheet(\\\"Site Effects\\\")\\nnxt = write_df(ws, site_df, title=f\\\"Per-Site Treatment Effects (ANCOVA, ITT/LOCF). Outlier site: {outlier_site}\\\")\\nwrite_df(ws, loso_df, start_row=nxt, title=\\\"Leave-One-Site-Out Sensitivity Analysis (Primary Endpoint)\\\")\\n\\n# Sheet 3: Subgroup Forest\\nws = wb.create_sheet(\\\"Subgroup Forest\\\")\\ninter_df = pd.DataFrame([\\n    {\\\"Interaction Term\\\": \\\"Treatment x Age Group (<65 vs >=65)\\\", \\\"P-value\\\": float(int_age_p),\\n     \\\"Significant (a=0.05)\\\": \\\"Yes\\\" if int_age_p < 0.05 else \\\"No\\\",\\n     \\\"Clinical Interpretation\\\": (\\\"Effect modification by age; review subgroup sizes and consistency\\\" if int_age_p<0.05 else \\\"No evidence of effect modification by age; treatment effect consistent across age groups\\\")},\\n    {\\\"Interaction Term\\\": \\\"Treatment x Sex\\\", \\\"P-value\\\": float(int_sex_p),\\n     \\\"Significant (a=0.05)\\\": \\\"Yes\\\" if int_sex_p < 0.05 else \\\"No\\\",\\n     \\\"Clinical Interpretation\\\": (\\\"Effect modification by sex; review subgroup sizes and consistency\\\" if int_sex_p<0.05 else \\\"No evidence of effect modification by sex; treatment effect consistent across sexes\\\")},\\n])\\nnxt = write_df(ws, inter_df, title=\\\"Mixed-Effects Model (Random Site Effect) - Interaction Terms\\\")\\nnxt = write_df(ws, sg_df, start_row=nxt, title=\\\"Subgroup Treatment Effects (ANCOVA within subgroup)\\\")\\nimg = XLImage(forest_png)\\nws.add_image(img, f\\\"A{nxt+1}\\\")\\n\\n# Sheet 4: Sample Size\\nws = wb.create_sheet(\\\"Sample Size\\\")\\nnxt = write_df(ws, ss_rows, title=\\\"52-Week Extension Sample Size Re-estimation (Chow, Shao & Wang two-sample parallel means)\\\")\\ncp_df = pd.DataFrame([\\n    {\\\"Metric\\\": \\\"Conditional Power at Week 24 (given observed data)\\\", \\\"Value\\\": f\\\"{cp*100:.1f}%\\\",\\n     \\\"Note\\\": \\\"Probability of rejecting H0 at final analysis given observed trend and planned N=480\\\"},\\n    {\\\"Metric\\\": \\\"Observed Z at current analysis\\\", \\\"Value\\\": round(obs_z,3), \\\"Note\\\": \\\"\\\"},\\n    {\\\"Metric\\\": \\\"Observed pooled SD (%)\\\", \\\"Value\\\": round(sd,3), \\\"Note\\\": \\\"\\\"},\\n    {\\\"Metric\\\": \\\"Observed overall effect (%)\\\", \\\"Value\\\": round(eff_full,3), \\\"Note\\\": \\\"ANCOVA, ITT/LOCF\\\"},\\n])\\nwrite_df(ws, cp_df, start_row=nxt, title=\\\"Conditional Power of Current Study\\\")\\n\\n# Sheet 5: RWE Comparison\\nws = wb.create_sheet(\\\"RWE Comparison\\\")\\na1c_out = a1c_by_adm.reset_index().rename(columns={\\n    \\\"adm_label\\\":\\\"Admission Type\\\",\\\"sum\\\":\\\"A1C Tested (n)\\\",\\\"count\\\":\\\"Encounters (n)\\\",\\\"pct_tested\\\":\\\"% A1C Tested\\\"})\\na1c_out[\\\"% A1C Tested\\\"] = a1c_out[\\\"% A1C Tested\\\"].round(2)\\nnxt = write_df(ws, a1c_out, title=\\\"A1C Testing Proportions by Admission Type - UCI Diabetes 130-US Hospitals (1999-2008)\\\")\\nnxt = write_df(ws, rwe_med_rows, start_row=nxt, title=\\\"Medication Utilization: RWE Cohort vs DX24-301 Baseline History\\\")\\n\\nfor ws in wb.worksheets:\\n    for col in range(1, ws.max_column+1):\\n        maxlen = 0\\n        for row in range(1, ws.max_row+1):\\n            v = ws.cell(row, col).value\\n            if v is not None:\\n                maxlen = max(maxlen, min(len(str(v)), 60))\\n        ws.column_dimensions[get_column_letter(col)].width = max(12, maxlen+2)\\n\\nwb.save(OUT)\\nprint(\\\"OUTLIER_SITE\\\", outlier_site)\\nprint(\\\"OVERALL_EFF\\\", round(overall_eff,4), \\\"p=\\\", f\\\"{overall_p:.3e}\\\")\\nprint(\\\"EXCL_EFF\\\", round(eff_excl,4), \\\"p=\\\", f\\\"{p_excl:.3e}\\\")\\nprint(\\\"POOLED_SD\\\", round(sd,4))\\nprint(\\\"INT_AGE_P\\\", f\\\"{int_age_p:.4f}\\\", \\\"INT_SEX_P\\\", f\\\"{int_sex_p:.4f}\\\")\\nprint(\\\"COND_POWER\\\", f\\\"{cp*100:.1f}%\\\")\\nprint(\\\"N_FULL per arm\\\", n_full, \\\"total\\\", tot_full)\\nprint(\\\"N_EXCL per arm\\\", n_excl, \\\"total\\\", tot_excl)\\nprint(\\\"Saved:\\\", OUT)\\n\", \"filePath\": \"/workspace/task/analysis.py\"}","call_id":"write_0_2bc39dcb","name":"write","type":"function_call","id":null,"status":null,"namespace":null},{"call_id":"write_0_2bc39dcb","output":"Wrote file successfully.","type":"function_call_output","id":null,"status":null},{"arguments":"{\"command\": \"cd /workspace/task && python3 analysis.py\", \"description\": \"Run full integrity analysis\", \"timeout\": 300000}","call_id":"bash_0_10b38266","name":"bash","type":"function_call","id":null,"status":null,"namespace":null},{"call_id":"bash_0_10b38266","output":"Traceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/workspace/task/analysis.py\", line 115, in <module>\n    mm = smf.mixedlm(\n         ^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.11/dist-packages/statsmodels/regression/mixed_linear_model.py\", line 1137, in from_formula\n    mod = super().from_formula(formula, data, *args, **kwargs)\n          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.11/dist-packages/statsmodels/base/model.py\", line 210, in from_formula\n    tmp = handle_formula_data(data, None, formula, depth=eval_env, missing=missing)\n          ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.11/dist-packages/statsmodels/formula/formulatools.py\", line 70, in handle_formula_data\n    result = mgr.get_matrices(\n             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.11/dist-packages/statsmodels/formula/_manager.py\", line 533, in get_matrices\n    output = patsy.dmatrices(\n             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.11/dist-packages/patsy/highlevel.py\", line 317, in dmatrices\n    (lhs, rhs) = _do_highlevel_design(\n                 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^