       -   [Income & Expense Trackers](https://excelx.com/template/income-expenses/)\n    -   [Calendar Templates](https://excelx.com/calendars/)\n        -   [2027 Calendars](https://excelx.com/template/calendar/2027y/)\n        -   [2026 Calendars](https://excelx.com/template/calendar/2026y/)\n        -   [2025 Calendars](https://excelx.com/template/calendar/2025y/)\n        -   [All Calendar Templates](https://excelx.com/calendars/)\n-   [Premium Templates](https://analysistabs.org/?utm_source=xlx&utm_medium=mmenu)\n-   [](# \"Search\")\n\nSearch for: \n\n# Download Free Finance & Accounting Sample Data for Excel\n\n1.  [Home](https://excelx.com)\n2.  [Practice Center](https://excelx.com/practice-data/)\n3.  Download Free Finance & Accounting Sample Data for Excel\n\n-   [![Free Finance and Accounting Data for Excel Practice Workbooks](https://excelx.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Finance-and-Accounting-Data-for-Excel-Practice-Workbooks.png)](https://excelx.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Finance-and-Accounting-Data-for-Excel-Practice-Workbooks.png)\n\n**Download free Excel workbooks** and master financial reporting with five fully-synthetic, audit-ready **Finance & Accounting datasets**—General Ledger, Accounts Payable, Accounts Receivable, Budget Forecast and Expense Claims. Each file mimics real-world workflows yet is 100 % dummy data, perfect for practicing PivotTables, Power Query, Power BI, variance analysis, ageing schedules and audit trails—no sign-ups, no compliance worries.\n\n## 1\\. General Ledger Dataset\n\nTwo thousand balanced journal lines spanning revenue, COGS and expense accounts. Ideal for building trial balances, P&L statements and drill-down ledger explorers. Every entry includes department, cost center and multi-currency codes so you can practice segment reporting and currency conversions without touching a live ERP.\n\n![Finance and Accounting Data General Ledger Dataset](https://excelx.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Finance-and-Accounting-Data-General-Ledger-Dataset.png)\n\n> **Columns Included:**  \n> `GLID`, `TxnDate`, `AccountNumber`, `AccountName`, `Debit`, `Credit`, `Dept`, `CostCenter`, `Description`, `Currency`\n\n-   Create trial balance PivotTables.\n-   Build department-level P&L dashboards.\n-   Test multi-currency conversions.\n-   Audit journal entries with Power Query.\n\n[Download General Ledger (.xlsx)](https://excelx.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/General-Ledger.xlsx)\n\n## 2\\. Accounts Payable Dataset\n\nEight hundred vendor invoices featuring due dates, currencies, payment status and terms. Use it to build ageing schedules, track cash-flow impact of payables or practice VLOOKUP joins with vendor master lists. Status flags let you highlight open versus paid liabilities in seconds.\n\n![Finance and Accounting Data Accounts Payable Dataset](https://excelx.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Finance-and-Accounting-Data-Accounts-Payable-Dataset.png)\n\n> **Columns Included:**  \n> `APID`, `Vendor`, `InvoiceDate`, `DueDate`, `Amount`, `Currency`, `Status`, `PaidDate`, `Terms`\n\n-   Create AP ageing buckets (30/60/90 days).\n-   Analyse cash-flow requirements.\n-   Match invoices to payments.\n-   Graph top vendors by spend.\n\n[Download Accounts Payable (.xlsx)](https://excelx.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Accounts-Payable.xlsx)\n\n## 3\\. Accounts Receivable Dataset\n\nNine hundred customer invoices with due dates and receipt status for practicing collection KPIs, DSO calculations and customer ageing reports. Pair it with the General Ledger to reconcile AR control accounts or build a cash-collection forecast.\n\n![Sample Finance and Accounting Data Accounts Receivable Dataset](https://excelx.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Sample-Finance-and-Accounting-Data-Accounts-Receivable-Dataset.png)\n\n> **Columns Included:**  \n> `ARID`, `Customer`, `InvoiceDate`, `DueDate`, `Amount`, `Currency`, `Status`, `ReceivedDate`, `Terms`\n\n-   Compute Days Sales Outstanding (DSO).\n-   Build AR ageing charts.\n-   Reconcile AR to GL balances.\n-   Highlight overdue invoices automatically.\n\n[Download Accounts Receivable (.xlsx)](https://excelx.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Accounts-Receivable.xlsx)\n\n## 4\\. Budget Forecast Dataset\n\nThis workbook holds quarterly budgets, forecasts and actuals for six departments across two fiscal years. Practise variance analysis, waterfall charts and rolling forecasts. Perfect for FP&A learners who need realistic numbers without sharing real financials.\n\n![Sample Finance and Accounting Data Budget Forecast Dataset](https://excelx.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Sample-Finance-and-Accounting-Data-Budget-Forecast-Dataset.png)\n\n> **Columns Included:**  \n> `FiscalYear`, `Dept`, `Quarter`, `BudgetUSD`, `ForecastUSD`, `ActualUSD`, `VarianceUSD`, `Notes`\n\n-   Visualize budget vs actual variances.\n-   Create department KPI scorecards.\n-   Build rolling-forecast formulas.\n-   Analyze year-over-year growth.\n\n[Download Budget Forecast (.xlsx)](https://excelx.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Budget-Forecast.xlsx)\n\n## 5\\. Expense Claims Dataset\n\nOne thousand employee claims for travel, meals and supplies with approval flows and multi-currency amounts. Practice conditional-format workflows, build dashboards for policy compliance or test Power Query merges with employee master data.\n\n![Sample Finance and Accounting Data Expense Claims Dataset](https://excelx.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Sample-Finance-and-Accounting-Data-Expense-Claims-Dataset.png)\n\n> **Columns Included:**  \n> `ClaimID`, `EmployeeID`, `SubmitDate`, `Category`, `Description`, `Amount`, `Currency`, `Status`, `ApprovedBy`, `PayDate`\n\n-   Flag claims over policy limits.\n-   Create approval funnel charts.\n-   Analyse spend by category or employee.\n-   Reconcile paid claims to GL postings.\n\n[Download Expense Claims (.xlsx)](https://excelx.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Expense-Claims.xlsx)\n\n## Conclusion & Next Steps\n\nUse these Finance & Accounting workbooks to build ageing schedules, P&L dashboards, variance waterfalls or audit-ready ledgers—risk-free. Bookmark this page and revisit each quarter for fresh numbers. Looking for other business functions? Head back to the [Main Sample Data Library](/practice-data/) to explore HR, Sales, Manufacturing and more.\n\n### 2 Comments\n\n1.  **Ganesh prasad Navajith kumar** May 24, 2026 at 12:36 am [- Reply](#comment-11541)\n    \n    Get me an live calss\n    \n    -   **PNRao** June 11, 2026 at 1:12 am [- Reply](#comment-11699)\n        \n        We appreciate the request! Right now, we focus on providing practice data and don’t host live classes. However, we recommend joining our community to get updates in case we start offering them in the future!\n        \n\n### Leave A Comment [Cancel reply](/practice-data/finance-accounting/#respond)\n\nComment\n\n  \n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment.\n\n  \n\n [![120+ Premium Project Management Templates](https://excelx.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/Premium-Project-Management-Templates.png)](https://analysistabs.org/?utm_source=xlx&utm_medium=wcta)[Save 85%\n\n120+ Premium Project Management Templates ★ Trusted in 100+ countries ✓ Instant download ✓ Lifetime updates Get templates →](https://analysistabs.org/?utm_source=xlx&utm_medium=wbanner) [\n\n**80+** PREMIUM\n\n#### Budget, Finance,  \nCalendars & Life  \nPlanner Templates\n\n→ Get Premium Templates\n\n+ Budget & Planner Templates\n\n+ Debt & Net Worth Trackers\n\n+ Calendars & Event Trackers\n\n+ Life Planners & Habit Trackers\n\n+ Life OS™ Bundle — Save 80%\n\n**Take Control of Your Finances**  \nInteractive dashboards, auto-calculations & visual breakdowns — starting from just $9.\n\n\n\n](https://analysistabs.org/budget-finance/?utm_source=xlx&utm_medium=wcta)[\n\n💰 Save 80%\n\n80+ Premium Budget, Calendar & Life Planner Templates ★ Trusted in 100+ countries ✓ Instant download ✓ Lifetime updates Get templates →](https://a