(with their GL_IDs) plus adjustment rows (AJE-xx/CE-xx) so subtotals match the Schedule C draft. Notes column explains multi-currency caveat etc.\n\nWait, but should CSV be only GL rows? \"mapping every Q1 expense from the GL to its Schedule C line\" — yes, every GL Q1 expense row must appear. Including adjustment rows makes the grand total match the Schedule C. I'll include them, clearly flagged in Notes. Good.\n\nSubtotals per line:\n- Line 4 COGS (Part III): 39,143.94 (39 rows)\n- Line 24a Travel: 38,334.50 (41 rows) + CE 970.98 = 39,305.48\n- Line 26 Wages: 40,230.09 (44 rows) + CE 10,769.91 = 51,000.00\n- Line 20b Rent: CE 9,600.00\n- Line 25 Utilities: CE 1,275.00\n- Line 15 Insurance: CE 468.75\n- Line 22 Supplies: CE 16,036.85\n- Line 27b Other (bank charges): AJE 105.00\nGrand total expenses = 157... let me compute: 39,143.94+39,305.48+51,000+9,600+1,275+468.75+16,036.85+105 = 156,935.02. And Schedule C line 28 = line 28 above 117,791.08 + COGS? No — line 28 excludes COGS (line 4 is in Part I). Line 28 = 39,305.48+51,000+9,600+1,275+468.75+16,036.85+105 = 117,791.08 ✓. Grand total in CSV = line 4 + line 28 = 156,935.02. Consistent.\n\nVendor audit sheet: \n- Cross-reference table: 7 bank vendor withdrawals vs AP:\n  1. CHK-1401 1/10 ABC 2,204.28 → AP10758 (inv 1/10, 2,204.28 USD, Paid 2/9) — amount match; date mismatch: check cleared 30 days before AP PaidDate → exception (possible misdated PaidDate or duplicate payment risk given CHK-1402).\n  2. CHK-1402 2/9 ABC 1,847.50 → no AP invoice match → unmatched payment exception (investigate; possible unauthorized/partial payment; note PaidDate of AP10758 is 2/9 but amount differs by 356.78).\n  3. CHK-1403 2/15 ABC 2,005.72 → AP10362 exact ✓.\n  4. CHK-1404 2/27 Global 3,133.53 → AP10452 exact ✓.\n  5. CHK-1405 3/18 BluePrints 2,302.71 → AP10108 exact ✓.\n  6. CHK-1406 3/28 Global 4,543.11 → AP10581 exact ✓.\n  7. EFT-2210 2/10 Fast Travel 970.98 → AP10274 amount match but status still Open → exception (AP not 