; −117708.53 = 141778.83. adj_cash = 142596.39 − 817.44 = 141778.95. Hmm mismatch 0.12? Let me recompute gl_cash_before: 95000 + 221925.41 − 117708.53 = 199216.88? No: 95000+221925.41=316925.41; 316925.41−117708.53 = 199216.88. I earlier wrote 142596.39 — wrong! Let me recompute: 221925.41 − 117708.53 = 104216.88. 95000+104216.88 = 199216.88. So gl_cash_before = 199216.88, not 142596.39. I made an arithmetic error earlier (I must have mistyped). Then adj = 199216.88 − 817.44 = 198399.44. But adjusted bank = 141778.83. Difference = adjusted_bank − book = 141778.83 − 198399.44 = −56620.61. Hmm, that's because the bank side should use net cash-basis items differently. Let me redo the reconciliation logic.\n\nProper reconciliation:\nBank side: balance per bank + deposits in transit − outstanding checks = adjusted bank.\nBook side: balance per books + interest − charges − NSF = adjusted book.\n\nIf books recorded full accrued revenue (221925.41) and accrued expenses (117708.53) as cash flows, then book cash before adj = 199216.88.\n\nBank received: deposits 27887.22 + interest 37.56 = 27924.78 total credits.\nBank paid: 85362.83 total debits (incl svc 105, NSF 750).\n\nBank → book direction: adjusted bank = bank_end + DIT − OC. We need adjusted bank = adjusted book = 199216.88 − 817.44 = 198399.44.\n\nSo DIT − OC = 198399.44 − 37561.95 = 160837.49. So DIT = 221925.41 (revenue not deposited... wait, revenue accrued but only 27887.22 deposited, so uncollected revenue = 221925.41 − 27887.22 = 194038.19) and OC: expenses accrued but unpaid. Cash outflows recorded in books but not through bank? Book expenses 117708.53; bank outflows 85362.83 (of which svc 105 and NSF 750 are book adjustments, and interest 37.56 is book adjustment on the deposit side).\n\nLet me think carefully. Reconcile bank to book:\n\nBook cash before adj = 95000 + GL revenue 221925.41 − GL expenses 117708.53 = 199216.88.\nBook adjustments: +37.56 (interest), −105 (svc), −750 (NSF) → adjusted book 198399.44.\n\nBank balance = 37561.95 = 95000 + 27924.78 − 85362.83.\n\nReconciling items (bank → book):\nAdjusted book − bank = 198399.44 − 37561.95 = 160837.49.\n\nDecompose:\n- Revenue accrued in books but not deposited: 221925.41 − 27887.22 (deposits excl. interest) = 194038.19 → deposits in transit (uncollected AR).\n- Expenses accrued in books but not paid: book expenses 117708.53; bank withdrawals excl. svc+NSF = 85362.83 − 855 = 84507.83. Unpaid accrued expenses = 117708.53 − 84507.83 = 33200.70 → outstanding checks.\n- Check: DIT − OC = 194038.19 − 33200.70 = 160837.49. ✓\n\nSo correct figures: DIT = 194,038.19; Outstanding checks = 33,200.70. My earlier numbers double-counted the actual bank activity. I need to fix: gl_cash_before = 199216.88, dep_transit = 194038.19, out_checks = 33200.70, adjusted = 198399.44.\n\nSanity: bank withdrawals excl svc/NSF 84507.83 = rent 9600 + util 1275 + ins 1875 + loan 3750 + travel 970.98 + checks 16036.85 + payroll 51000 = 84507.83 ✓.\n\nUpdate the script accordingly: adjusted_bank = 37561.95 + 194038.19 − 33200.70 = 198399.44; adj_cash = 199216.88 − 817.44 = 198399.44 ✓.\n\nAlso update exception texts amounts: EXC-001 amount 221925.41 with description noting only 27,887.22 collected → DIT 194,038.19. EXC-002: accrued expenses 117,708.53, unpaid portion 33,200.70. Fix workbook labels: deposits in transit = 194,038.19; outstanding = 33,200.70. AJE effect text: GL cash 199,216.88 − 817.44 = 198,399.44.","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning","encrypted_content":null,"content":null},{"arguments":"{\"filePath\": \"/tmp/build_deliverables.py\", \"oldString\": \"bank_end = 37561.95\\ndep_transit = 221925.41      # accrued revenue recorded in GL, not yet collected\\nout_checks = 117708.53       # accrued expenses recorded in GL, not yet paid\\nadjusted_bank = round(bank_end + dep_transit - out_checks, 2)  # 141,778.83\\n\\nint_income = round(12.45 + 11.89 + 13.22, 2)  # 37.56\\nsvc_charges = 105.00\\nnsf = 750.00\\ngl_cash_before =