,{"index":1,"criterion":"Each exception must have all required columns: Exception_ID (unique identifier), Source_File (which file the discrepancy was found in), Reference (transaction reference number), Description (clear explanation), Amount (dollar amount), Resolution (action taken or recommended), and Status (Resolved or Unresolved)","passed":true,"reasoning":"All rows in the CSV include the required columns: Exception_ID, Source_File, Reference, Description, Amount, Resolution, and Status.","evidence":"Header line contains all seven column names and each data row (EXC-001 through EXC-013) has seven comma‑separated values."}],"overall_reasoning":"Criterion 0 fails because not all major discrepancies are represented; criterion 1 passes. Since both criteria must pass, the rubric does not pass."}},{"index":9,"rubric":"Does the Schedule C Draft worksheet (Sheet 4 of the Reconciliation Workbook) correctly replicate the Schedule C structure with Part I (Income) including Line 1 gross receipts of $40,557.62 and Part II (Expenses) with line-level amounts that tie back to the expense summary?","weight":10,"result":{"passed":false,"score":0,"criteria_count":3,"criteria_passed":1,"criteria_results":[{"index":0,"criterion":"Sheet 4 must replicate the IRS Schedule C structure with Part I Income showing Line 1 Gross receipts (combined Sales Revenue $23,318.47 + Online Sales $17,239.15 = $40,557.62), Line 4 COGS ($4,421.20), Line 5 Gross Profit ($36,136.42), Line 6 Other income (Interest Income $37.56), and Line 7 Gross income ($36,173.98)","passed":false,"reasoning":"The Schedule C Draft shows Line 1 Gross receipts of $221,925.41 (GL 4000 Sales Revenue $124,585.69 + 4010 Online Sales $97,339.72) and Line 4 COGS of $39,143.94, which do not match the required $40,557.62 gross receipts, $4,421.20 COGS, $36,136.42 gross profit, $37.56 other income, and $36,173.98 gross income specified in Criterion 0.","evidence":"Schedule C Draft – Line 1: 221925.41; Line 4: 39143.94; Line 5: 182781.47; Line 6: 37.56; Line 7: 182819.03."},{"index":1,"criterion":"Part II Expenses must include amounts for Line 15 (Insurance), Line 20b (Rent $9,600.00), Line 24a (Travel $7,534.42), Line 25 (Utilities $1,275.00), Line 26 (Wages), and Line 27a (Other expenses—bank charges $105.00)","passed":false,"reasoning":"The Draft lists Line 15 Insurance as $1,875, Line 24a Travel as $38,334.50, and Line 27a Other expenses as $4,033.74, whereas Criterion 1 requires Insurance $105, Travel $7,534.42, and Other expenses $105. Rent and Utilities match, but the other required lines do not.","evidence":"Schedule C Draft – Line 15: 1875; Line 20b: 9600; Line 24a: 38334.5; Line 25: 1275; Line 26: 40230.09; Line 27a: 4033.74."},{"index":2,"criterion":"The amounts must be internally consistent and tie back to the Q1_2024_Schedule_C_Expense_Summary.csv","passed":true,"reasoning":"The amounts in the Draft for Lines 15, 20b, 24a, 25, 26, and 27a correspond exactly to the totals listed in the Q1_2024_Schedule_C_Expense_Summary.csv, indicating internal consistency and correct mapping.","evidence":"Schedule C Draft – Line 15: 1875 (CSV: 1875); Line 20b: 9600 (CSV: 9600); Line 24a: 38334.5 (CSV: 38334.5); Line 25: 1275 (CSV: 1275); Line 26: 40230.09 (CSV: 40230.09); Line 27a: 4033.74 (CSV: 4033.74)."}],"overall_reasoning":"Criterion 0 and Criterion 1 are not satisfied because the Schedule C Draft uses the full Q1 GL amounts rather than the specified $40,557.62 gross receipts and the smaller expense figures. Criterion 2 is internally consistent with the expense summary, but the overall rubric fails because not all criteria passed."}}],"task_dir":"/Users/cmunley/Documents/Codex/2026-09-02/g/work/Gym/cache/huggingface/hub/datasets--JobBench--job-bench/snapshots/7ff2673ac78f42e492b204f5fffe0b8ccc11bf7d/dataset/bookkeeping_accounting_and_auditing_clerks/task1","rubrics_file":"/Users/cmunley/Documents/Codex/2026-09-02/g/work/Gym/cache/huggingface/hub/datasets--JobBench--job-bench/snapshots/7ff267