1 = 9,810.15 from reversing/recording all unmatched items.\n\nAlternatively simpler presentation for the book side: group adjustments:\n- Add: unrecorded bank deposits (net of erroneous recorded revenue)\n- etc. Let me compute:\n\nCash book revenue recorded: 45,650. Actual bank deposits: 29,780 + 3.21 interest. Cash book expenses recorded: 45,918.71. Actual bank withdrawals: 20,368.76 (incl. duplicate 187.50).\n\nNet cash per book change: 45,650 − 45,918.71 = −268.71. Actual net: 29,783.21 − 20,368.76 = +9,414.45. Difference = 9,414.45 − (−268.71) = 9,683.16. Hmm: adjusted book = 24,318.72 + 9,683.16 = 34,001.88 (bank balance, without Verizon addback). Then plus Verizon 187.50 → 34,189.38 → 9,870.66 total. Consistent.\n\nFor presentation, book side adjustments grouped:\n1. Add: Interest earned 12/31: +3.21\n2. Deduct: Bank service charges (12/27 $25 + 12/31 $15): −40.00\n3. Correct State Farm (recorded 452.00, actual 425.00): +27.00\n4. Correct Duke Energy (recorded 214.78, actual 214.50): +0.28\n5. Correct Staples (recorded 127.43, actual 124.35): +3.08\n6. Record unrecorded Staples purchase 12/31: −42.88\n7. Correct City Water (recorded 87.32, actual 780.00): −692.68\n8. Correct check #1086 (recorded Al's Auto 1,287.50; actual Mike's Auto 485.00): +802.50\n9. Reverse cash book receipts never deposited & record actual deposits (net): 29,780 − 45,650 = −15,870\n10. Reverse cash book disbursements never cleared & record actual unrecorded disbursements (net): compute. Actual withdrawals excl. those already covered by items 2-8 and duplicate Verizon: 20,368.76 − 40 (fees) − 425 (StateFarm) − 214.50 (Duke) − 124.35 − 42.88 (Staples) − 780 (City Water) − 485 (Mike's) − 187.50 (dup Verizon) = 20,368.76 − 2,299.23 = 18,069.53. Book disbursements excl. items corrected in 2-8: 45,918.71 − 452 − 214.78 − 127.43 − 87.32 − 1,287.50 = 43,749.68. Net adjustment = 43,749.68 − 18,069.53 = +25,679.68? Wait sign: reversing book disbursements increases cash; recording actual ones decr