 paid 12/3 ✓; December's second 4,850 paid 12/17; wages for period 12/16-12/29 accrued but unpaid → note accrued payroll payable for accountant. AP end ADP = 0 (or accrued liability not yet invoiced — mention in memo).\n\nAP roll-forward table:\nVendor | Opening 11/30 | New Dec invoices | Dec payments | Ending 12/31 | Notes\nSiteOne 456.80 | 0 | 456.80 | 0\nPremier 890.00 | 1,520.00 | 1,250.00 | 1,160.00\nHome Depot 342.17 | 342.17(new INV-0400) | 342.17 | 342.17 — flag\nDuke 214.50 | 214.50 | 214.50 | 214.50 — flag\nComcast 129.99 | 129.99 | 129.99 | 129.99 — flag\nMike's 485 | 485 | 485 | 485 — flag\nJohn Deere 567 | 567 | 567 | 567 — flag\nState Farm 425 | 425 | 425 | 425 — flag\nADP 4,850 | 4,850 (Dec period est) | 9,700 | 0 — hmm. ADP Dec new: second payroll 4,850. 4,850+4,850−9,700=0 ✓\nHarrison 450 | 450 | 450 | 450 — flag\nWaste Mgmt 165 | 0 | 165 | 0\nAcme 325 | 0 | 0 | 325 — disputed\nShell Oil 0 | 78.54 | 78.54 | 0\nLowe's 0 | 287.63 | 287.63 | 0 (12/23 93.47 debit card purchase not invoiced — direct purchase; could add. Keep to invoiced items + note)\nVerizon 0 | 187.50 | 187.50 | 0 (plus duplicate 187.50 refund receivable)\nMeta 0 | 250 | 250 | 0\nDaily Herald 0 | 175 | 175 | 0\nCity Water 0 | 780 | 780 | 0\nGreenfield Properties 0 | 1,800 | 1,800 | 0\nAce Hardware 0 | 215 | 0 | 215\nElite Tree 0 | 1,100 | 0 | 1,100\n\nTotals: opening 9,300.46 ✓; ending 4,413.66+... sum ending: 0+1160+342.17+214.50+129.99+485+567+425+0+450+0+325+0+0+0+0+0+0+0+215+1100 = 5,413.66. Earlier I had 5,413.66 ✓ (with ADP 0).\n\nPayments total: opening payments: 456.80+1250+342.17+214.50+129.99+485+567+425+9700+450+165+0+78.54+287.63+187.50+250+175+780+1800 = let me not bother; the sheet will compute.\n\nNow Schedule C line names (2024): confirm via fetch. Let me try.\n\nThen write the build script. Number formats, professional layout. Let me write the code.\n\nFor the Reconciliation sheet:\nBANK SIDE:\nBalance per bank statement 12/31/2024: 34,001.88\nAdd: Bank error — duplicate Verizon Wireless ACH debit 12/11 (refund pending): 187.50\nAdd: Deposits in transit: 0.00\nSubtotal: 34,189.38\nLess: Outstanding checks: 0.00\nAdjusted bank balance: 34,189.38\n\nBOOK SIDE:\nBalance per cash book 12/31/2024: 24,318.72\nAdd: Interest earned: 3.21\nAdd: Correction — State Farm overstatement: 27.00\nAdd: Correction — Duke Energy overstatement: 0.28\nAdd: Correction — Staples overstatement: 3.08\nAdd: Correction — check #1086 recorded at 1,287.50, actual 485.00: 802.50\nAdd: Net correction — disbursements recorded in cash book that never cleared vs. actual unrecorded bank disbursements: 25,680.15\nLess: Bank service charges (25.00 + 15.00): (40.00)\nLess: Unrecorded Staples purchase 12/31: (42.88)\nLess: Correction — City Water recorded 87.32, actual 780.00: (692.68)\nLess: Net correction — receipts recorded but never deposited vs. actual deposits: (15,870.00)\nAdjusted book balance: 34,189.38\n\nGreat, ties.\n\nLet me fetch the IRS Schedule C PDF to confirm line names, then build.","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning","encrypted_content":null,"content":null},{"id":"msg_0cd247bd56df4f89a273702912bd66f9","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"All source data reviewed. Now let me verify the official 2024 Schedule C line items from the IRS.","type":"output_text","logprobs":null}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":null},{"arguments":"{\"url\": \"https://www.irs.gov/pub/irs-prior/f1040sc--2024.pdf\", \"format\": \"text\"}","call_id":"webfetch_0_7fc0f57e","name":"webfetch","type":"function_call","id":null,"status":null,"namespace":null},{"call_id":"webfetch_0_7fc0f57e","output":"%PDF-1.7\r%����\r\n1320 0 obj\r<</Linearized 1/L 108238/O 1325/E 29509/N 2/T 107722/H [ 510 344]>>\rendobj\r            \r\n1342 0 obj\r<</DecodeParms<</Columns 4/Predictor 12>>/Filter/FlateDecode/ID[<60847BB37539C243AFD88359D5474F7A><EEDA0920BF5D5A46BFA264761CB91347>]/Index[1320 46]/Info 1319 0 R/Length 103/Prev 107723/Root 1321 0 R/Size 1366/Ty