k Ads, Daily Herald, NAPA Auto Parts, AT&T, and Staples, which is required by criterion 1. Therefore the overall rubric does not pass."}},{"index":7,"rubric":"Does the management memo state the adjusted true cash balance and report the total count of reconciling items, consistent with the reconciliation worksheet?","weight":6,"result":{"passed":false,"score":0,"criteria_count":4,"criteria_passed":2,"criteria_results":[{"index":0,"criterion":"The variance memo must include the adjusted true cash balance — the single figure that both the adjusted bank balance and adjusted book balance reconcile to.","passed":false,"reasoning":"The memo lists two different figures for the adjusted balances: $20,188.19 for the bank side and $16,677.99 for the book side. The true cash balance should be a single figure that both sides reconcile to, but the memo does not provide such a single figure.","evidence":"Memo: \"Adjusted bank balance (true cash) .................  $20,188.19\" and \"Adjusted cash book balance ........................  $16,677.99\"; Reconciliation sheet: ADJUSTED BANK BALANCE 20,188.19, ADJUSTED CASH BOOK BALANCE 16,677.99."},{"index":1,"criterion":"The memo must report the count of reconciling items identified.","passed":false,"reasoning":"The memo does not provide a total count of all reconciling items. It only mentions the count of outstanding checks (21) and lists individual items, but no overall reconciling item count is given.","evidence":"Memo: \"Outstanding checks (21)\"; no aggregate reconciling item count is stated."},{"index":2,"criterion":"The memo must distinguish between bank-side reconciling items (outstanding checks, deposits in transit, duplicate charges) and book-side reconciling items (unrecorded bank charges, book errors, omissions).","passed":true,"reasoning":"The memo clearly separates bank-side reconciling items (e.g., outstanding checks, duplicate Verizon charge) from book-side reconciling items (e.g., unrecorded bank fees, book-error corrections).","evidence":"Memo sections: bank side items – \"Outstanding checks (21)\" and \"Duplicate Verizon charge\"; book side items – \"Unrecorded bank fees\" and \"Book-error corrections\"."},{"index":3,"criterion":"The stated true cash balance must match the Reconciliation sheet of December_2024_Month_End_Close.xlsx.","passed":true,"reasoning":"The true cash balance stated in the memo ($20,188.19) matches the value in the Reconciliation sheet of the Excel file.","evidence":"Memo: \"Adjusted bank balance (true cash) .................  $20,188.19\"; Reconciliation sheet: ADJUSTED BANK BALANCE (true cash), 12/31/2024, 20188.19."}],"overall_reasoning":"The rubric fails because criteria 0 and 1 are not satisfied. The memo does not provide a single true cash balance reconciled by both sides, nor does it report a total count of reconciling items. Criteria 2 and 3 are met, but all criteria must pass for the rubric to pass."}}],"task_dir":"/Users/cmunley/Documents/Codex/2026-09-02/g/work/Gym/cache/huggingface/hub/datasets--JobBench--job-bench/snapshots/7ff2673ac78f42e492b204f5fffe0b8ccc11bf7d/dataset/bookkeeping_accounting_and_auditing_clerks/task2","rubrics_file":"/Users/cmunley/Documents/Codex/2026-09-02/g/work/Gym/cache/huggingface/hub/datasets--JobBench--job-bench/snapshots/7ff2673ac78f42e492b204f5fffe0b8ccc11bf7d/dataset/bookkeeping_accounting_and_auditing_clerks/task2/RUBRICS.json","task_source":"job_bench_opencode_agent","_ng_task_index":3,"_ng_rollout_index":0,"agent_ref":{"name":"job_bench_opencode_agent"}}
