====================================================================\n43: 3. DESIGN CRITERIA\n44: ===============================================================================\n45: \n46: Design Loading:\n47: - AASHTO HL-93 Live Load\n48: - Earth Load per AASHTO LRFD Bridge Design Specifications\n49: \n50: Concrete Requirements:\n51: - Compressive Strength (f'c): 5,000 psi at 28 days\n52: - Exposure Class: Class II (moderately aggressive environment)\n53: - Minimum Cover: 2 inches (clear cover to reinforcement)\n54: \n55: Reinforcing Steel:\n56: - Grade 60 (fy = 60,000 psi)\n57: - Epoxy-coated for all reinforcement\n58: \n59: Hydraulic Design:\n60: - Design Flow (Q100): 850 cfs\n61: - Headwater Depth: 7.2 feet maximum\n62: - Outlet Velocity: 8.5 fps\n63: \n64: ===============================================================================\n65: 4. PRECAST SEGMENT DETAILS\n66: ===============================================================================\n67: \n68: Segment Configuration:\n69: - Number of Segments: 9 segments\n70: - Segment Length: 8 feet each (standard)\n71: - Joint Type: Bell and spigot with rubber gasket\n72: \n73: Wing Walls:\n74: - Type: Cast-in-place reinforced concrete\n75: - Height: 6 feet (varies)\n76: - Length: 12 feet each side (inlet and outlet)\n77: - Wall Thickness: 12 inches\n78: \n79: Headwalls:\n80: - Type: Cast-in-place reinforced concrete\n81: - Inlet and Outlet: 10-inch thick parapet walls\n82: \n83: Apron Slabs:\n84: - Inlet Apron: 8 feet x 14 feet x 8 inches thick\n85: - Outlet Apron: 12 feet x 14 feet x 10 inches thick\n86: - Riprap: Class III, 18-inch thick, 150 SF at outlet\n87: \n88: ===============================================================================\n89: 5. EARTHWORK REQUIREMENTS\n90: ===============================================================================\n91: \n92: Excavation:\n93: - Structure Excavation: Estimated 1,850 cubic yards\n94: - Foundation Preparation: Compact to 95% relative density\n95: \n9